WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.560
Most big rivers of the Peninsula

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.900
run east.

3
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.460
These ones went the other way.

4
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.520
They did not leave a note.

5
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:09.930
Three questions.

6
00:00:10.657 --> 00:00:12.097
Question one.

7
00:00:12.097 --> 00:00:14.657
Most Peninsular rivers drain

8
00:00:14.657 --> 00:00:16.437
into the Bay of Bengal.

9
00:00:16.437 --> 00:00:18.457
Which of these drains into the

10
00:00:18.457 --> 00:00:20.117
Arabian Sea instead?

11
00:00:20.117 --> 00:00:22.657
Mahanadi. Kaveri.

12
00:00:22.657 --> 00:00:24.127
Tapi. Krishna.

13
00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:27.686
Three. Two. One.

14
00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:29.728
The Tapi.

15
00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:32.408
It rises in the Satpura ranges

16
00:00:32.408 --> 00:00:33.808
and runs west.

17
00:00:33.808 --> 00:00:36.028
The other three flow east and

18
00:00:36.028 --> 00:00:37.418
make deltas.

19
00:00:37.839 --> 00:00:38.919
Question two.

20
00:00:38.919 --> 00:00:41.119
The Narmada and the Tapi flow

21
00:00:41.119 --> 00:00:43.439
west along a landform made by

22
00:00:43.439 --> 00:00:45.279
faulting. What is it?

23
00:00:45.279 --> 00:00:46.439
Rift valley.

24
00:00:46.439 --> 00:00:47.799
Delta plain.

25
00:00:47.799 --> 00:00:49.139
Coastal lagoon.

26
00:00:49.139 --> 00:00:50.289
Hanging valley.

27
00:00:50.796 --> 00:00:53.666
Three. Two. One.

28
00:00:54.796 --> 00:00:56.456
A rift valley.

29
00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.396
The Tapi runs parallel to the

30
00:00:58.396 --> 00:01:01.366
Narmada, in a rift of its own.

31
00:01:01.916 --> 00:01:03.156
Question three.

32
00:01:03.156 --> 00:01:05.556
What do the Narmada and the Tapi

33
00:01:05.556 --> 00:01:07.836
make where they meet the sea?

34
00:01:07.836 --> 00:01:10.036
Deltas. Estuaries.

35
00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.786
Lagoons. Fjords.

36
00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:15.648
Three. Two. One.

37
00:01:16.272 --> 00:01:18.592
Estuaries. They are the only

38
00:01:18.592 --> 00:01:21.012
long rivers flowing west, and

39
00:01:21.012 --> 00:01:23.122
they do not build deltas.

40
00:01:24.278 --> 00:01:24.845
For GS1:

41
00:01:24.845 --> 00:01:27.138
the Western Ghats are the water

42
00:01:27.138 --> 00:01:30.058
divide. The Narmada and the Tapi

43
00:01:30.058 --> 00:01:32.398
flow west, in rift valleys, into

44
00:01:32.398 --> 00:01:33.428
estuaries.
